cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Research compendium for "Mapping the AI Research of China, the US and the EU"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software and
  the associated article.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Pigeon-Effect/qss_publication
abstract: >-
  Complete research compendium for a scientometric analysis of citation shares
  within AI subdisciplines, derived from 1,986,659 OpenAlex records (2020-2025):
  keyword construction, OpenAlex data collection, dataset quality control, a
  semi-supervised hierarchical topic model (SPECTER embeddings, K-Means
  over-segmentation, expert consolidation) yielding 5 domains, 31 fields and 106
  research fronts, fractional citation-share analysis across that taxonomy for
  China, the US and the EU-27, visualization, and LLM-based external validation
  of the taxonomy by document intrusion detection, adapted from the "reading tea
  leaves" paradigm of Chang et al. (2009) and run for 1,000 trials at each of the
  three hierarchy levels. Includes the complete record of all 3,000 validation
  trials, the cluster-level citation-share tables, and the manuscript sources.
keywords:
  - scientometrics
  - topic modeling
  - cluster validation
  - intrusion detection
  - large language models
  - OpenAlex
  - artificial intelligence
  - citation analysis

